Well if you buy new books, you will only be able to get D&D, as they dropped
the A in the last upgrade. If you get the books make sure you get the
version 3.5 as it is more balanced. The newest edition of D&D has this nifty
thing called an open gaming license. Which means any company can produce
material using that system. Hey kind of like nethack. In any case there is a
lot of stuff out there that is better then what wizards put out. There is
also a lot of worse stuff.

Honestly if your group is in money troubles and you still want to play you
can get away with an investment of about 100$. If you don't mind sharing the
price about 4 people or so it's not bad.
You need 1 copy of
Players handbook
Dungeon Masters Guide
Monster manual.
1 set of dice. Its a pain but you can share if you don't want to spend the
money.

Also there are newsgroups dedicated to D and D
rec.games.frp.dnd for example but this is the last question I would ask
there as it is kind of treated like "Who is better Jesus or Allah".

You can also email me, I've played of 17 years, mostly as a DM and I love
